From c771a8916e90f01786e2d743b0f774b73eacf7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:45:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] macOS: Build Proton's Wine on x86_64 macOS (Rosetta 2)
 with WoW64.

Guard Linux-only Proton additions so the tree builds and runs on
macOS, leaving Linux behaviour unchanged:

- fsync: futex syscalls only on Linux, ENOSYS elsewhere (fsync is
  never enabled without futex support).
- ntsync: include ntsync_tmp.h only on Linux so the existing
  non-ntsync fallback is used.
- ntdll: malloc.h/mallopt(M_PERTURB) only with glibc; set_thread_teb()
  only uses arch_prctl on Linux (macOS sets %gs per thread in
  init_syscall_frame); stub sysfs helpers for WINE_CPU_TOPOLOGY.
- ntdll: use "jmp *%rcx" for the indirect jump, which clang requires.
- amd_ags_x64: make libdrm/amdgpu optional.
- win32u: inactive fshack framebuffer surface stubs without EGL.
- media-converter: include pthread.h explicitly.
- configure: disable loader64 on Darwin.
- server: derive the user SID from the hardware UUID on macOS
  instead of /etc/machine-id.
- Regenerate server protocol files with tools/make_requests.

